    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Abbasids overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyads</a> in 750 and ruled a multi-ethnic Islamic empire from their new capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-wisdom">House of Wisdom</a> translated Greek, Persian and Indian learning into Arabic and helped give the world <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algebra">algebra</a>.</li><li>Turkic slave soldiers, then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buyid-dynasty">Buyid</a> and Seljuk overlords, hollowed out caliphal power long before the Mongols sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> in 1258.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The word '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algebra">algebra</a>' comes from al-jabr in the title of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-khwarizmi">al-Khwarizmi</a>'s treatise on calculation, written in Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> around 820.</p></aside>
    </section>

